From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tests: do not require experimental fixed-address mappings

MDB_FIXEDMAP is documented by LMDB as highly experimental and may fail when
the operating system cannot reserve the requested virtual address. RISC-V
QEMU reports EOPNOTSUPP for this optional mapping mode, aborting the test
sequence before its transaction and cursor checks run.

The mtest programs do not rely on stable pointer addresses. Use the regular
mapping mode while retaining every transaction, duplicate-key, cursor, and
split test.

diff --git a/libraries/liblmdb/mtest.c b/libraries/liblmdb/mtest.c
--- a/libraries/liblmdb/mtest.c
+++ b/libraries/liblmdb/mtest.c
@@ -50 +50 @@ int main(int argc,char * argv[])
-		E(mdb_env_open(env, "./testdb", MDB_FIXEDMAP /*|MDB_NOSYNC*/, 0664));
+		E(mdb_env_open(env, "./testdb", 0, 0664));
diff --git a/libraries/liblmdb/mtest2.c b/libraries/liblmdb/mtest2.c
--- a/libraries/liblmdb/mtest2.c
+++ b/libraries/liblmdb/mtest2.c
@@ -53 +53 @@ int main(int argc,char * argv[])
-	E(mdb_env_open(env, "./testdb", MDB_FIXEDMAP|MDB_NOSYNC, 0664));
+	E(mdb_env_open(env, "./testdb", MDB_NOSYNC, 0664));
